{
  "_comment": "EXAMPLE Pulse job registry. Copy this to $MINERU_HOME/config/launchd-jobs.json (or point MINERU_LAUNCHD_JOBS_FILE at it) and edit for your install. The web app's Pulse tab reads it via app/launchd_jobs.py to title each launchd job and locate its freshness signal. Schema: each job is keyed by label_suffix (the part after LAUNCHD_LABEL_PREFIX, e.g. 'morning-brief' -> 'com.mineru.morning-brief'). freshness.kind is one of: newest_in_dir (needs dir, optional exclude[]), file_mtime (needs path), neutral (no artifact). dir/path/exclude are relative to MINERU_HOME. Jobs without a freshness block (always-on daemons) fall back to their plist log mtime. Edit display_name freely; keep label_suffix aligned to your actual plist labels and trigger scripts.",
  "jobs": [
    {"label_suffix": "morning-brief", "display_name": "Morning Briefing", "freshness": {"kind": "newest_in_dir", "dir": "briefs_morning"}},
